sub("19.5. ChatGPT, second reading. Adopted: each crossing of the commission marked between agents (15.2), and the downstream sequence set out (15.3); the seven letters called a distributed configuration with no order claimed (11.5),",
    "19.5. ChatGPT, second reading. Adopted: each crossing of the commission marked between agents (15.2), and the downstream sequence set out (15.3); the seven letters called a distributed configuration with no order claimed (11.5; superseded in v1.1 by 11.5b),")
after_para("19.8. ", "19.9. Version 1.1 (2026-11-11). The occasion: a ChatGPT composition of v1.0, supplied by the author on 2026-11-11, which carried the paper's hedges faithfully; the hedges were the paper's. The author's points, each checked against the seats before anything was changed: \"why the hell is that not relatively obvious literary dependence? why does it pass in hebrews but get hedged around here where the transform dependence is much stronger and clearer?\" (0.5, 16.4a, 16.7, 17); \"i think the haran gawaita material has not been mapped appropriately - they have the seven too, and seven communities - its an interpretive key for revelation, not just a random comparison\", with \"it *offers* itself as a text that is an interpretive key, and unveiling of the secret history\" and the method, \"taking the haran gawaita on its own terms, applying it in an obvious way to revelation that maps directly, and seeing what it yields up\" (13.0, 13.6, 11.5a); \"the way the reception history is treated, it makes it seem like there is no sequence in the seven mapping\" (11.5, 11.5b, 16.6); \"i also feel like we can make the joshua Jesus and logos connection stronger... and is zechariah talking to the son of nun? is that not a different joshua?\" (2.6, 4.1a, 4.3, 4.5, 7a.8, 7a.9); \"it is highly significant that philo withholds the name at that precise moment\" (4.4); \"is the stanping and naming in philo sufficiently linked to the white stone?\" and \"thats the socket. a name only the one who receives it will know. the socket in philo is the reader supplying the name of the missing referent, jesus\" (4.4a, 7b.1, 7b.9, 7b.10). Wolfson (16.5b) enters at the author's word of 2026-11-10, with the reading of his paper made in session. Found in the seats while answering: Zech 3:4, 3:7, 3:8, 3:9 (the robe, the midst, the second Ἀνατολή oracle, the stone with seven eyes), Ezek 9:2, Wis 18:24, Exod 33:11, Acts 26:10, Ovid, Met. 15.41–42, Justin, Dial. 115–116.")

